      "writtenOn": "2022-02-03T08:15:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "LGTM.\n\nNote that the rules prevent shrinking of annotations and generic signatures (assuming a default Proguard config is keeping them using a -keepattributes rule) from any kept item (which seems to be quite many). We may want to expose a way in R8 to avoid that, similarly to \u0027,allowaccessmodification\u0027. This is related to b/190469643.\n\nAlso, it may be worthwhile checking that the default Proguard config (if any) is not keeping runtime invisible annotations (e.g., using -keepattributes *Annotations*).",
